{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1221065-adamantine-arrow-thyrsus-legacy-the-vajra","id":1221065,"title":"Adamantine Arrow/Thyrsus Legacy: the Vajra","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-21T21:24:52-07:00","id":1221065,"title":"Adamantine Arrow/Thyrsus Legacy: the Vajra","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>Legacy: The Vajra</u></i></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Vajra are old, their Legacy dating back into antiquity during Alexander\u2019s march of conquest and the origin of the Thunderbolt Warriors. At a time when man pushed further, and the Awakened of the world first began to come together, the Vajra charged forward. They declared that Truth was found in conflict, and for that end stood at the front lines and in the secret corners, seeking men and gods to test themselves against. They walked among them, and when the time was right struck with the sudden ferocity of the heavens, their very souls made into weapons.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In the modern day, the Thunderbolts try to claim responsibility for the birth of the Adamantine Arrow. They\u2019ve certainly been its constant companion as far back as anyone has recorded, drawing almost the entirely of their membership from the Order. Despite this, they\u2019ve not wholly tethered themselves to it; Truth is in conflict, and the Legacy welcomes any who would see it explored at the end of a blade or the tip of an arrow. Sometimes a martially-inclined Guardian will seek out the Legacy, or a Thearch better at swordpoint diplomacy. The Mysterium rarely joins, though its members sometimes seek to study the Vajra\u2019s techniques, and the Free Council is all but unheard of. Non-Arrow members typically have trouble among their own Orders. The teachings of the Thunderbolts skew so heavily towards the beliefs of the Arrow that many caucuses consider joining philosophically compromising.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Thunderbolts traditionally prefer simple martial weapons and the bow-and-arrow. This has not stopped some members from attempting to develop their skills along unorthodox lines, utilizing complicated throwing weapons or complex weaponry. While not taught by the Legacy, there are even rumors of more modern members shaping their souls into modern firearms.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once a Vajra reaches their fourth attainment, they choose a signature weapon. In response, their Nimbus changes to reflect this new Truth. Colors might become sharp like a dagger, they might hear the sounds of steel swords slamming together, or there might come the ominous sensation of the approach of the headsman\u2019s axe. They can then take and shape their Nimbus into a weapon, their personal Astra. These are never just weapons, they are part of the Vajra's soul, and are often named and conceived of before achieving the fourth attainment in the belief that they're not creating a weapon but instead taking hold of what was always there.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Sobriquet:</i> Thunderbolts</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Parent Path and Order:</i> Thyrsus, Adamantine Arrow</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Ruling Arcanum:</i> Prime</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Yantras:</i> Wound penalties (+1 to +3, equal to penalty), striking an enemy (+1), meditating before a fight (+2), thunderstorms (+2)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Oblations:</i> Sparring, honoring a defeated foe, researching or engaging in military strategy, cleaning or performing maintenance on a weapon</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Initiation</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Requirements:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Prime 2; Spirit 1; Melee, Brawl, or Athletics 2; a weapon-based combat Specialty; a War Specialty in Academics or Politics</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Initiation is simple: the prospective Thunderbolt must approach or be approached by one of the Vajra. They are questioned and tested on both their knowledge of combat and the philosophy of war. If their mentor is satisfied, the student then reshapes their Nimbus and its Tilt in alignment with martial combat, either to bolster their allies or weaken their enemies.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Attainments</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Initiation: Gaze Pierces the Dark Clouds</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The first thing to learn isn\u2019t how to strike, but to know where to. With a hard look, the Thunderbolt can assess the strengths and weaknesses of others. This replicates the Prime spell \u201cSupernal Vision.\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Optional: Spirit 1</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Man or god, both are tests. In addition to the above, the attainment also replicates the Spirit spell \u201cKnow Spirit.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Second: From the Clear Sky</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Prerequisites:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Prime 2, Stealth 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thunder is sudden. The Thunderbolt can walk among his peers, innocuous, until the time comes to strike. This replicates the Prime spell \u201cCloak Nimbus.\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Optional:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Spirit 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">After striking, the light, heat and noise vanish just as quickly as they came. This replicates the Spirit spell \u201cShadow Walk.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Third: A Soul Like Diamond</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Prerequisites: </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prime 3, Athletics 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Having learned where to strike, the Thunderbolt now prepares himself for the act. This replicates the Prime spell \u201cWards &amp; Signs\u201d for a scene.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Optional:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Spirit 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Even the gods have difficulty following the lightning. In additon to the above, the Thunderbolt also benefits from effects of the Spirit spell \u201cEphemeral Shield.\u201d </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Fourth: I Am The Astra</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Prerequisites: </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prime 4; Melee, Brawl, or Athletics 4; a weapon-based combat specialty</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At this level, the Thunderbolt learns the signature skill of the Legacy: to become their chosen weapon. Upon learning this Attainment, the Thunderbolt chooses a signature weapon from their weapon specialties; the bow-and-arrow is a popular choice. The Thunderbolt\u2019s Nimbus vanishes and appears in their hand as a weapon, their Astra (see below), which lasts for a scene.</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The signature weapon for their Astra can be changed, but only in two ways: altering the Thunderbolt\u2019s Nimbus tilt through rising in Gnosis, or by abstaining from using it for a month as they dedicate themselves to another weapon specialty.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Optional: Spirit 4</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With a swipe of their Astra, the Thunderbolt can rend apart the Gauntlet to strike sudden, to vanish as quickly as he struck, or to confront enemies normally out of reach. This replicates the effects of the Spirit spell \u201cReaching,\u201d with extra Reach applied to opening Irises across the Gauntlet.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Fifth: Thunder Breaks the Silence</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Prerequisites:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Prime 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thunder rattles the world and makes even the dedicated flinch. Having learned of his enemies, and having mastered himself, the Thunderbolt turns to the arena. This spell replicates the Prime spell \u201cDisplay of Power,\u201d with extra Reach applied to rote Counterspelling. The Vajra sometimes insist they were the first to conceive of and use the spell.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Optional: Spirit 5</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Thunderbolt dictates the terms of engagement even to the gods. With the swipe of a weapon, he severs their ties to the world as the Spirit spell \u201cBanishment,\u201d with extra Reach applied to blocking re-establishing Conditions until Duration lapses.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>The Astra</b><br /> Uses the Thunderbolt's signature weapon as mechanical template, save as follows.<br /> DMG [Gnosis/2 round up]; Init 0; Str N/A<br /> Size and Special as appropriate for the weapon<br /> If ranged, Range as appropriate for the weapon<br /> If ranged, Clip is infinite and draws ammunition from Mana at a rate of 1=1; doesn't leave shells, arrows, or otherwise behind<br /> <br /> The Astra can be used as a +2 yantra tool, and can be made the Mage's Dedicated Tool.<br /> The Astra is obviously magical, reflecting truths of the Mage's Nimbus.<br /> Unless suppressed by spell or by <i>From the Clear Sky</i>, everyone nearby is subject to the full persistent force of the Mage's Nimbus Tilt.<br /> The Mage's Nimbus fades from his person and becomes embodied in the Astra. Spellcasting can still be read and Counterspelled as normal by watching the way the Astra flares in Active Mage Sight.<br /> The Mage's Nimbus returns to his person the moment he lets go of the Astra. He can be disarmed, but can summon the Astra again per the usual Instant Action. If the Astra is thrown, it vanishes once it hits or fails to hit its target.<br /> The Astra can be disguised or enchanted after summoning by spells of Forces and of the five Subtle Arcana. This is often used to make the Astra appear like a normal weapon or to transfigure it into elemental fire or lightning, and to make it a better yantra tool or weapon.<br /> <br /> <b><i>While the Astra is summoned, all spells not using the Astra as a yantra or not cast on the Astra itself require an extra Reach to cast, as imagoes struggle to form through the Mage's dissociated Gnosis.</i></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Removed the Astra spell, instead makings it its own weapon with its own unique properties and restrictions.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I also snuck in the possibility for some smarty-pants modern guy to use this Legacy with guns. It'd just require learning everything traditionally, then deciding to have your Astra be made from your pistol specialty. Which would probably be frowned on, and if anyone has done it it's probably a so-rare-as-to-maybe-be-nonexistent Free Council member.<br /> <br /> I allowed Forces to affect Astra weapons because it felt wrong that they couldn't make their Astras actual thunderbolts if they felt so inclined, and so that Astras could be disguised.<br /> <br /> The attainments and their yantras synergize well with Adamant Hand. This is intentional.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":13241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","user":"Biston","date":". 05-22-2018, 04:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T23:36:57-07:00","id":1221089,"title":"","content":"That Astra spell looks a lot like a Patterning spell (Prime 4). <br /> <br /> Or you could just make it a unique thing not based on a spell. That way you don\u2019t need to worry about things like spell factors and Reach. <br /> <br /> If you want to keep it as a Prime 3 spell, then perhaps it\u2019s better as a variant of the Platonic Form spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T23:44:05-07:00","id":1221090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1221065-adamantine-arrow-thyrsus-legacy-the-vajra?p=1221089#post1221089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That Astra spell looks a lot like a Patterning spell (Prime 4).<br /> <br /> Or you could just make it a unique thing not based on a spell. That way you don\u2019t need to worry about things like spell factors and Reach.<br /> <br /> If you want to keep it as a Prime 3 spell, then perhaps it\u2019s better as a variant of the Platonic Form spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually meant to type Patterning. And yeah, it's honestly its own thing, I mostly farted it out for formatting's sake. Didn't need to be a spell, I should've just made a statblock for it.. If I'd made it a real spell, half of what it did would've ended up Reach effects which feel needlessly and pointlessly restrictive conceptually for the Vajra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T00:31:33-07:00","id":1221096,"title":"","content":"Alright, chucked the spell and wrote up the Astra as a weapon with some clarifications and emphases. Thank you for your advice, 21C Hermit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}